# Normalise line endings in the REPOSITORY, on commit, for every text file.
#
# Why this exists in a fresh module: without it, what gets stored depends on each
# contributor's core.autocrlf -- which on Windows is set by the Git installer's
# SYSTEM config, not by anything in the repo. It works until someone clones with a
# different default and their next commit rewrites whole files as a line-ending
# change, burying the real diff. `text=auto` makes it explicit and machine-
# independent: text files are LF in git, whatever the working tree does.
#
# It deliberately does NOT set `eol=lf`. That would force an LF WORKING TREE too,
# and a FlexSim module contains files whose consumers may not tolerate it -- your
# <Module>.fsx is parsed by FlexSim's own cmdloadtree. Leaving eol unset keeps the
# normal Windows checkout behaviour.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: any generator that writes LF will make git report
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" on a CRLF working
# tree. That warning is COSMETIC -- the committed blob is clean LF either way.
# Do not chase it. DO check `git diff --numstat` when a diff looks unexpectedly
# large: a genuine line-ending rewrite shows up as +N/-N across the whole file.
#
# Mark genuinely binary payloads explicitly so `text=auto` never guesses at them.
* text=auto

# --- binary: never normalise, never diff as text ---
*.dll   binary
*.lib   binary
*.exp   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.cur   binary
*.t     binary
